%% Render: ~/.zcode/tools/mermaid-render/render.sh -i firing-handoff.mmd -o ../images/firing-handoff.png -b white -s 2 -w 1600
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Watching
    Watching --> Firing: absent from the latest scan
    Watching --> Firing: outside top-3 in two scans
    Watching --> Firing: two losing closes in a row
    Watching --> Firing: leader wallet silent 8h
    Watching --> Firing: 12h with nothing open
    Watching --> Firing: fresh board, no open position
    Firing --> Handoff: unsigned intents cancelled
    Handoff --> Watching: next candidate hired
    Handoff --> Paused: no acceptable candidate
    Paused --> Watching: fresh shortlist or manual pick
    note right of Watching : a winning unit resets the loss count, a breakeven leaves it unchanged. The rank rule stands down when the newest scan is older than 2h
    note right of Firing : a rotation only fires when nothing is open. There is no cooldown, a fired trader is hireable again the moment they qualify
    state "Watching the trader" as Watching
    state "Firing, atomically" as Firing
    state "Handoff" as Handoff
    state "Paused, waiting for ZCode" as Paused
